  place  support for businesses and what labor is  saying is we would be putting in place a  contingency fund of a billion pounds for  energy intensive businesses in addition  to that we would be raising the  threshold at which business rates are  paid  before then actually reforming business  rates and we'd be raising that money  from an increase in the digital services  tax we've got to be helping households  we've got to be helping businesses as  well  um i'm also interested to uh know  your take on whether or not there might  be an early election there has been a  bit of speculation is labor on an  election footing  we are absolutely on an election footing  and i want to see this government swept  away as soon as possible these are  continuity candidates and part of the  conservative debate over the summer has  been about all the problems that have  been caused by 12 years of conservative  rule to sweep this government away we  need to have that general election and  we in labor want to see that general  election happen as soon as we possibly  can so we can get on with the job of  rebuilding our country's economy and  standing beside people in this acute  cost of living crisis that looks like  it's only going to get worse in the  months ahead  we spoke to lord lister also earlier on  the program of course someone who's been  very close to boris johnson for a long  time and he said  that he wouldn't rule out a return  to frontline politics for boris johnson  if the ball came loose at the back of  the scrum he wouldn't rule anything out  do you think that boris johnson  could come back  it really does show the depths to which  the conservative party has sunk and the  fact they are so  tired after 12 years in office that  they've just ousted  a  leader after his flagrant disregard for  kovid rules after he showed time and  again it was one rule for him and  another rule for the rest of the  population it really does show now the  conservative party has completely lost  its way if they they are saying credibly  that they want to get rid of one leader  then try to have a leadership contest  with others then try and bring the other  leader back the only way we're ever  going to get a fresh start is to sweep  the conservatives away completely  okay thank you very much indeed nick  thomas simmons there for the labour  party
 

